=== meta ===
rule: CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED
title: a comment in a JS test kept under .github/workflows/ is test code, not a weakened command
origin: ruling 197.Q5 (2026-10-03) - a file that carries test obligations is not scanned as shell: the test rules judge its lines. v0.5.0 read the added comment as `npm test || true` and blocked at high; no assertion changed, so only the warn remains
=== before: .github/workflows/gen.test.ts ===
import { test, expect } from "vitest";
import { total } from "./value";
test("total", () => { expect(total()).toBe(78.75); });
test("other", () => { expect(total()).toBe(78.75); });
=== after: .github/workflows/gen.test.ts ===
import { test, expect } from "vitest";
import { total } from "./value";
test("total", () => { expect(total()).toBe(78.75); });
test("other", () => { expect(total()).toBe(78.75); });
// npm test || true
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED", "severity": "warn"}]
